Rule 1 (tensor shapes should be the same)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 2 (v_2 should be a valid dimension of input tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= -1 × ndim(v_1) ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ ndim(v_1) - 1
>>
Rule 5 (tensor must have at least 2 dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 6 (tensor must be a valid dimension)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0
>>
Rule 7 (tensor must have at least one dimension that is positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 2) > 0
